## PART 7 — discovery-service: Consumer Worker

Each replica runs a consumer worker that reads from the stream and
processes one application at a time with a distributed lock.

```
1. Log LogConsumerStarted with replicaID.

2. Start stale reclaim goroutine (runs independently):
   Every coord.Config.StaleClaimInterval:
   - coord.Stream.ClaimStale(
         ctx,
         constants.StreamOperations,
         constants.ConsumerGroupName,
         replicaID,
         coord.Config.StaleClaimMinIdle,
         xwareredis.StreamStaleClaimMaxCount,
     )
   - For each reclaimed message:
       state = coord.State.Get(cycleID)
       if state != nil &&
          state.Status == "in_progress" &&
          state.StartedAt != nil &&
          time.Since(*state.StartedAt) > coord.Config.StaleClaimMinIdle:
           coord.State.UpdateStep(cycleID, StepFailed, "failed")
           coord.Stream.Ack(...)
           coord.Dedup.Release(...)
           log(LogConsumerStaleReclaimed, messageID)
       else:
           process normally via message handling below.

3. Main consumer loop (blocking, runs forever):

   messages = coord.Stream.Consume(
       ctx,
       constants.StreamOperations,
       constants.ConsumerGroupName,
       replicaID,
       coord.Config.BatchSize,
       coord.Config.BatchBlockDuration,
   )

   For each message:

   a. Parse appName, namespace, cycleID, operation, attempts from fields.
      log(LogConsumerProcessing, appName, attempts)

   b. If attempts >= coord.Config.MaxRetryAttempts:
        coord.State.UpdateStep(cycleID, StepFailed, "failed")
        coord.Stream.Ack(...)
        coord.Dedup.Release(...)
        log(LogConsumerMaxAttempts, appName)
        continue.

   c. lockKey   = constants.KeyPrefixLockApp + appName
      lockValue = replicaID + ":" + cycleID

   d. coord.State.UpdateStep(cycleID, StepAcquiringLock, "in_progress")

   e. acquired = coord.Lock.Acquire(
          ctx, lockKey, lockValue, coord.Config.LockTTL)
      → false: log LogConsumerLockNotAcquired.
               Do NOT ack — leave in PEL.
               continue to next message.

   f. coord.State.Set: status=in_progress, startedAt=now,
                       replicaId=replicaID, step=StepProcessing.

   g. Start lock heartbeat goroutine:
      hbCtx, cancelHB := context.WithCancel(ctx)
      defer cancelHB()
      go func() {
          ticker := time.NewTicker(coord.Config.LockHeartbeatInterval)
          defer ticker.Stop()
          for {
              select {
              case <-ticker.C:
                  ok, err := coord.Lock.Extend(
                      hbCtx, lockKey, lockValue,
                      coord.Config.LockTTL)
                  if !ok || err != nil {
                      log(constants.LogConsumerLockLost, appName)
                      cancelHB()
                      return
                  }
              case <-hbCtx.Done():
                  return
              }
          }
      }()

   h. Dispatch to the correct handler based on operation type.
      Pass hbCtx — handlers must check ctx.Done() at each step
      and abort immediately if cancelled (lock lost):

      The agent must read the existing prewarm logic to discover
      which handlers exist and what each does. Wire them here.
      The handler executes the full per-application prewarm work
      that was previously done inline — change detection, snapshot
      creation, rollback check — in whatever order and structure
      the existing code uses. Do not restructure that logic.

   i. cancelHB()

   j. On handler success:
      coord.State.UpdateStep(cycleID, StepCompleted, "success")
      coord.Lock.Release(lockKey, lockValue)
      coord.Stream.Ack(...)
      coord.Dedup.Release(...)
      log(LogConsumerSuccess, appName)

   k. On handler error:
      log(LogConsumerFailed, appName, err)
      coord.Lock.Release(lockKey, lockValue)
      If attempts+1 < coord.Config.MaxRetryAttempts:
        Re-publish with attempts+1.
        coord.Stream.Ack(...)
      Else:
        coord.State.UpdateStep(cycleID, StepFailed, "failed")
        coord.Stream.Ack(...)
        coord.Dedup.Release(...)
        log(LogConsumerMaxAttempts, appName)
